From d2642e9adf26a06ec8aa8e5c075077fefde33271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:37:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a select has a selected option, submits it, and
 draws closed

An option's selectedness is its ElementState::CHECKED bit, as in Gecko,
so option:checked matches it. The mutator settles it when options come,
go, or have their selected attribute set or removed, by the selectedness
setting algorithm: an option inserted with selected is selected, one
whose attribute changes takes it (and, without multiple, unselects the
others), and a select without multiple then has exactly one, the last
selected or else the first that is not disabled. There is no script, so
there is no dirtiness. An embedder picks an option as the user does
(pick_option), and reads the options, their values and the select's.

Form data has each selected option that is not disabled, under the
select's name.

A select without multiple draws closed, as browsers draw it: the selected
option and an arrow, as wide as its widest option (every option sits in
one grid cell, the others hidden). Its list is not drawn.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
